STEP 4 -- prune on leave, graft on re-join (19:09:56-19:11:36; 11346-pg1-*, -pg2-*, -s4-pruned-*)
  11346-prunegraft.sh (tools/): a 40 s stream at 1000 pps, IGMPv2 Leave at +10 s, report at
  +25.8 s. Every received frame is timestamped (tb470 /tmp/ck12/rx-pg{1,2}.txt, 25 K lines each,
  not committed).
                              pg1 (19:09:56)       pg2 (19:11:04)
    sent                      40,001               40,001
    received                  25,247               25,290
    before the leave          9,893 frames         9,894 frames
    last frame after leave    +2.598 s             +2.566 s
    gap                       14.755 s             14.712 s
    first frame after join    +1.581 s             +1.568 s
    after the join            12,755 frames        12,829 frames
    other gaps (max)          1 ms                 3 ms
  received = sent - the gap in both runs, so there was no loss outside the prune window.
  While pruned: stack 19:10:16 `show ip pim dense-mode mroute` -> "Downstream IF List: empty"
  and `show ip mroute` -> "Outgoing interface list:" (empty); the (S,G) stays, Upstream
  Forwarding. After the join: SA 19:10:24 IGMP group back (uptime 00:00:00), vlan3113 in
  'olist' again.
  -> the ~2.6 s stop is the SA's last-member query (2 x 1 s, `show ip igmp interface`) plus
     the PIM-DM prune; the ~1.6 s resume is the report plus the graft.

